      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Categorizing WHY media content is weak or strong gives sellers/analysts an actionable axis for improving satisfaction on media products, and 'not_applicable' correctly handles physical-product rows. Values are largely sound readings: AMZ-0003 'appallingly shallow' -> content_shallow_or_thin, AMZ-0005 praise -> high_quality_content. The AMZ-0002 'pacing_poor' label is a slightly loose fit (the complaint is about too much political commentary, not pacing per se), a minor grounding stretch but not an invention."
    },
    {
      "name": "product_category",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Product category is a strong grouping axis for the query: sellers can compare satisfaction drivers across books, music, DVDs, physical goods, etc. Values are well grounded in the text: baby doll -> physical_product_non_consumable, book review -> book_or_printed_media, music/artist -> music_cd_or_vinyl, Criterion film/DVD -> dvd_or_video. NULL used where category is unclear, which is appropriate. Well-warranted inferences throughout."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.88,
  "source_groundedness": 0.87,
  "rationale": "Both added columns provide genuine, distinct analytical axes (product type and content-quality failure mode) directly relevant to how sellers can improve satisfaction, neither being near-constant nor a trivial restatement of the original title/content fields. Values are generally sound readings of the source text with reasonable use of not_applicable/NULL for silent rows; the only weak spot is a somewhat loose 'pacing_poor' label on AMZ-0002, which is a minor grounding imperfection rather than a fabricated fact."
}

